(ned -- A PERPENDICULARITY, operator spec 2026-08-03.)
(MODEL. The rod slides DOWN PAST the puck at a standoff, then drives inward.)
(The puck does NOT need to extend downward: whatever station along the rod's)
(SHAFT is level with the puck makes contact, so every depth touches the SAME)
(feature with a DIFFERENT part of the rod. A vertical rod contacts at the)
(same Y at every depth; a rod tilted by A does not:)
(     recorded Y = constant - depth x tan A)
(The constant carries puck position, puck diameter, rod diameter and tip)
(centring, and it CANCELS in the difference. Both plunges are far below the)
(top, so the tip is clear of it and neither the tip's shape nor the puck)
(surface being out of perpendicular enters the measurement.)

(WHY DIVE DEEPER -- the resolution argument, and the math must honour it.)
(   tan of tilt = dY / dZ,  so  tilt = ATAN[dY]/[dZ])
(A touch repeats to about e, so the angle is uncertain by roughly e / dZ)
(radians.)
(Every extra mm of dZ buys resolution LINEARLY, and nothing else in the)
(expression depends on depth. That is the entire reason for going to -65.)
(   before  dZ = 35 mm  ->  5 um touch = 0.0082 deg)
(   after   dZ = 40 mm  ->  5 um touch = 0.0072 deg)
(CONSEQUENCE, and the reason this is spelled out: the two pairs have)
(DIFFERENT baselines, so their raw dY are NOT comparable -- a longer baseline)
(yields a larger dY for the very same tilt. Comparing dY would call a genuine)
(improvement a regression. The verdict is taken on the ANGLE, which is)
(baseline-independent, and both are reported.)

(SEQUENCE, operator spec -- no travelling between touches, it is wasted time.)
(  BEFORE: probe at -25, back off, plunge to -60 AT THE BACKOFF STANDOFF,)
(          probe again.          dZ = 35 mm)
(  CORRECT A.)
(  AFTER:  probe at -65, back off, rise to -25, probe again.)
(          dZ = 40 mm -- the deepest touch, so the verification is the)
(          sharpest measurement of the two.)
(  Then lower the puck and park on the zero pose with the corrected A.)

(REQUIRES: rod stickout greater than the deep plunge -- 65 mm -- or the shaft)
(no longer spans the puck and nothing is touched.)

(Results: #3050 = dY before, #3051 = dY after, #3052 = A correction applied,)
(         #3053 = tilt before deg, #3054 = tilt after deg.)
(#3069 accumulates every A correction: it IS where A's true zero now sits on)
(the DRO, so cal_c_zero tilts about it and every routine parks there.)

o<cal_a_zero> sub
  #<cx>    = #1        (setter centre X, work frame -- from #3045)
  #<cy>    = #2        (setter centre Y, work frame -- from #3046)
  #<top>   = #3        (setter top Z, work frame -- from #3047)

  #<d1> = 25.0         (before: shallow)
  #<d2> = 60.0         (before: deep)
  #<d3> = 65.0         (after: deep first)
  #<d4> = 25.0         (after: shallow)

  o5 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, CAL A: switch to MM first)
  o5 endif
  o6 if [#<top> EQ 0 AND #<cx> EQ 0 AND #<cy> EQ 0]
    (abort, CAL A: no setter centre - run StartPuck first)
  o6 endif

  (--- shared setup, GLOBAL so the file-level helper can read it -----------)
  #<_ca_cx>    = #<cx>
  #<_ca_cy>    = #<cy>
  #<_ca_top>   = #<top>
  (standoff mirrors cal_probe_center's r_out -- same clearance, same trip)
  #<_ca_stand> = 19.8
  (contact sits at radius 17.40, so 10 mm always trips first, and a)
  (no-contact fault stops 9.8 mm SHORT of centre instead of driving through)
  #<_ca_reach> = 10.0
  #<_ca_fpr>   = 100.0 (probe feed, operator spec)
  #<_ca_fla>   = 10.0  (latch feed, operator spec)
  #<_ca_ftr>   = 500.0 (traverse)
  #<_ca_fck>   = 200.0 (protective descent)
  (1 mm is plenty. A probe that will not release inside it is an ELECTRICAL)
  (contact fault -- fix the contact, not the distance. Operator 2026-08-03.)
  #<_ca_back>  = 1.0
  (clearance is 5 mm for every cal routine and IS the zero pose)
  #<_ca_safe>  = 5.0
  #<_ca_side>  = -1    (approach from -Y, probe toward +Y; +1 mirrors it)

  M50 P0               (pin the feed override -- probes run at programmed feed)
  M64 P3               (puck UP)
  G4 P1.5

  (=== BEFORE: -35, then -60 without leaving the standoff ==================)
  o<ca_touch> call [#<d1>] [1] [0]
  #<y1> = #<_ca_ty>
  o<ca_touch> call [#<d2>] [0] [0]
  #<y2> = #<_ca_ty>
  #<dy_b>   = [#<y2> - #<y1>]
  #<dz_b>   = [#<d2> - #<d1>]
  #<tilt_b> = [ATAN [#<dy_b>] / [#<dz_b>]]
  #3050 = #<dy_b>
  #3053 = #<tilt_b>
  (PRINT, CAL A BEFORE: y at -25 = #<y1>, y at -60 = #<y2>, DELTA Y = #<dy_b> over #<dz_b> mm, tilt #<tilt_b> deg)

  (=== CORRECT ============================================================)
  #<corr> = [0 - #<tilt_b>]
  #3052 = #<corr>
  (PRINT, CAL A: rotating A by #<corr> deg)

  o120 if [ABS[#<corr>] GT 5.0]
    G90
    G1 Z[#<top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
    M65 P3
    M50 P1
    (abort, CAL A: computed correction over 5 deg - refusing to swing the head that far on one measurement)
  o120 endif

  (Rotating in place is what saves the climb. It is only safe while the swing)
  (at the deepest point stays inside the standoff clearance: at 65 mm depth)
  (0.5 deg moves the tip 0.57 mm against 2.40 mm of clearance. Bigger)
  (corrections climb out first, and the next touch then re-approaches.)
  #<next_app> = 0
  o125 if [ABS[#<corr>] GT 0.5]
    G90
    G1 Z[#<top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
    #<next_app> = 1
    (PRINT, CAL A: correction #<corr> deg exceeds 0.5 - climbing clear before rotating)
  o125 endif
  G91
  G1 A#<corr> F600
  G90
  #3069 = [#3069 + #<corr>]

  (=== AFTER: -65, then rise to -25, same standoff ========================)
  o<ca_touch> call [#<d3>] [#<next_app>] [0]
  #<y3> = #<_ca_ty>
  o<ca_touch> call [#<d4>] [0] [1]
  #<y4> = #<_ca_ty>
  (deeper minus shallower, so the sign convention matches the BEFORE pair)
  #<dy_a>   = [#<y3> - #<y4>]
  #<dz_a>   = [#<d3> - #<d4>]
  #<tilt_a> = [ATAN [#<dy_a>] / [#<dz_a>]]
  #3051 = #<dy_a>
  #3054 = #<tilt_a>
  (PRINT, CAL A AFTER: y at -65 = #<y3>, y at -25 = #<y4>, DELTA Y = #<dy_a> over #<dz_a> mm, tilt #<tilt_a> deg)

  (=== puck DOWN, park on the zero pose with the corrected A ==============)
  G90
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
  M65 P3
  G4 P1.0
  G1 A#3069 C#3070 F600
  G1 X#<cx> Y#<cy> F[#<_ca_ftr>]
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<_ca_safe>] F[#<_ca_ftr>]
  M50 P1

  (=== verdict on the ANGLE, not on raw dY ================================)
  o130 if [ABS[#<tilt_a>] LT ABS[#<tilt_b>]]
    (PRINT, CAL A OK: tilt #<tilt_b> -> #<tilt_a> deg, A moved #<corr> deg. Sign is correct.)
    (DEBUG, CAL A: tilt #<tilt_b> to #<tilt_a> deg, A corrected #<corr> deg)
  o130 else
    (DEBUG, CAL A FAILED: tilt #<tilt_b> to #<tilt_a> deg - got WORSE. Flip side or the correction sign.)
    (abort, CAL A: correction made it WORSE - tilt #<tilt_b> then #<tilt_a> deg. The math or the sign is wrong. Failing loudly by design.)
  o130 endif

o<cal_a_zero> endsub

M2 (end program)
